    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG is delighted to present 4 Wilson Road, Mount Merrion a superb detached bungalow ideally suited to those seeking spacious living with ground floor accommodation, including three generously proportioned bedrooms complemented by a further two versatile and large attic rooms at first floor level making it an excellent choice for families, older couples, or anyone with a need for accessible and versatile accommodation.\n\nThis beautifully extended home is set on one of the largest and most private garden sites on the road, offering exceptional outdoor space with tremendous potential. The property has already been thoughtfully enhanced with a rear extension at both ground and first floor levels, incorporating modern design and high-quality finishes throughout, while retaining the charm and warmth of a traditional Mount Merrion bungalow.\n\nNestled in a quiet, leafy setting, 4 Wilson Road is a quiet residential road with little through traffic and enjoys the rare combination of tranquillity and convenience. Mount Merrion is a highly sought-after residential area, just a short distance from the City Centre, yet feels worlds away from the bustle of urban life. The area is known for its mature homes and generous gardens, and this property stands out for its outstanding rear garden again it is one of the largest on the road offering ample space for children to play, gardening, entertaining, or future expansion (subject to planning).\n\nThe main living accommodation is all on one level, designed with family life and ease of access in mind. A welcoming entrance hall with solid oak flooring offers a bedroom to the front on either side.\n\nThe heart of the home is the magnificent open-plan, L-shaped kitchen, dining and living area extending across the full width of the rear. Floor-to-ceiling glazing and dual patio doors flood the space with light and open directly onto a large raised deck, seamlessly connecting indoor and outdoor living. The modern kitchen is equipped with integrated appliances and ample storage, while the open-plan layout creates a perfect environment for family life and entertaining.\n\nAlso on the ground floor, another spacious double bedroom with built-in wardrobes and a large family bathroom with both bath and walk-in shower complete the single-level living experience ideal for those who value convenience and accessibility.\n\nUpstairs, the converted attic offers two additional large, dormer rooms, each with Velux windows, built-in storage, and wonderful garden views. The rear room features a charming Juliet balcony overlooking the expansive gardens with distant city views.\n\nOutside, the mature, private gardens are truly exceptional predominantly laid to lawn and bordered by established trees and shrubs, they offer both seclusion and significant potential. Whether you're dreaming of a garden office, a future extension, or simply want room to grow, the size and layout of this plot make it a rare find.\n\nThe detached garage adds further versatility, suitable for storage, a workshop, or conversion (subject to planning), enhancing the home's long-term potential. One of the two side entrances separate the house from the garage making it truly detached.\n\nIdeally located, Deer Park, a 32-acre public amenity together with UCD and its surrounding grounds are just a short walk away, offering scenic walks and fresh air on your doorstep. Excellent transport links include multiple bus routes (47, 11, 116, E1, S6 and more) nearby, with the Luas and DART also within easy reach. Major employers such as UCD, RTÉ, and St. Vincent's Hospital are all within walking distance, and local amenities including Supervalu, cafes, pharmacy, doctors, dentists and schools like Scoil San Treasa, St Andrew's and Mount Anville are close at hand. Plans to bring the Luas closer are underway, time will tell if they come to fruition or not.\n\nA rare opportunity to own a spacious, accessible family home with bedrooms at ground and first floor level, a modern layout, and one of the largest, most private gardens on Wilson Road offering immediate comfort and exciting future potential."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - 9m x 1.5m\nSpacious and inviting entrance hall, with the stairs hidden from view by an attractive area to the end. Timber floors. Accommodation off.\n\nLiving Room & Dining Room - 8.85m x 4.4m\nVery large open plan area with dual double doors leading to a raised deck within the rear garden. This room, an extension to the original footprint of the house is very generous in size, light filled and the ideal home reception area.\n\nKitchen - 3.8m x 3.5m\nFully fitted kitchen comprising a selection of floor and eye level fitted units with marble work surfaces, a tiled floor, double oven and gas hob. Door to side passage between the house and garage.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.8m x 3.5m\nFront facing bedroom (or additional reception room) with a Bay window, coving to the ceiling and a marble fireplace.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.5m x 3.35m\nFront facing double bedroom with Bay window. Coving. Coiuld be used as a reception room either.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.6m x 2.3m\nDouble bedroom with fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 3.45m x 2.2m\nRecently upgraded and comprising a bath, separate shower, toilet and wash hand basin. Tiled.\n\nLanding - 2.4m x 2.2m\nWith accommodation and shower room off.\n\nDormer Room 1 - 4.45m x 3.8m\nRear facing, large, versatile dormer room with Juliet balcony overlooking the expansive rear garden, twin Velux roof windows and built in storage space. TV point.\n\nDormer Room 2 - 4.85m x 3.8m\nDormer style, versatile dormer room with twin Velux roof windows and under eaves storage.\n\nShower Room - 3m x 1.4m\nShower, toilet and wash hand basin. Chrome radiator.\n\nGarage - 5.15m x 2.7m\nWith access from the driveway and out to the side passage.\n\nBoiler House - \nWith gas boiler.\n\nOutside Shed - 5m x 3m\n\n\nOutside - \nA pillared entrance opens to a large cobble-blocked driveway providing ample off street parking to complement the excellent, free, on-street parking available outside. Two gated side entrances lead from the front garden to the rear garden (c. 25m long x 20m wide) which is exceptionally large in size, mainly under lawns with boundaries of plants, trees and shrubs and a lovely, raised deck off the living and dining room areas. To the side is a large garage and additional storage shed. Generous in size this area is an excellent and valuable addition to the property and is versatile enough to continue as a garage or indeed as additional accommodation as an extension of the main dwelling or independent living (subject to Planning Permission).\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Outstanding detached bungalow on a large private site</li><li> Thee spacious bedrooms & 2 large converted attic rooms</li><li> Magnificent open-plan kitchen/living/dining room</li><li> Beautiful mature gardens</li><li> Large raised entertaining deck</li><li> Detached garage with future potential (subject to planning permission)</li><li> Excellent storage throughout</li><li> Prime residential location</li><li> Fantastic opportunity to further extend or develop (subject to planning permission)</li><li> Further external features include:</li><li> Two side entrances</li><li> Detached garage with excellent potential (subject to planning permission)</li><li> Additional garage / storage</li><li> Outside utility area</li><li> Extensive parking</li><li> Exceptional privacy</ul>"
      },
